.TH PATH_BASEPOS2 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
path_basepos2 \- Calculate the base position in a path

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/path_internal.h>
.IB #include <lib/utf8.h>

.IB size_t
.IB path_basepos2(const char* path, size_t len);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpath_basepos2\fR function calculates the base position in a given path. The base position is the position of the last directory separator in the path.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB path
The input path string.
.TP
.IB len
The length of the input path string.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the base position in the path. If no directory separator is found, the function returns the length of the input path.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBpath_basepos2\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/path_internal.h>
#include <lib/utf8.h>

int main() {
    const char* path = "/usr/lib";
    size_t len = strlen(path);
    size_t basepos = path_basepos2(path, len);
    printf("Base position: %zu\n", basepos);
    return 0;
}
.nef